<title>SPAIN: Spain's SEAT to halt production due French strike.</title>
<headline>Spain's SEAT to halt production due French strike.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volkswagen AG's Spanish unit SEAT said on Thursday it was halting production at its Martorell plant on Friday due to the blocked roads from a French truckers' strike, a SEAT spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>The factory makes 1,900 vehicles a day.</p>
<p>&quot;We are going to stop production starting tomorrow because of the strike in France,&quot; he said.  </p>
<p>He said SEAT had been forced in the past few days to import parts from Germany by air transport, but this had not been sufficient to maintain production.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2151</p>
</text>
